<td id="A0.T11.2.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.T11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">20 Epochs</td></tr>
<tr id="A0.T11.2.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Image Generation</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">FFHQ (Big U-Net, big_diffusion)</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">20</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" colspan="2">-</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.T11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">3 Epochs</td></tr>
<tr id="A0.T11.2.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Language Modeling</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">LLaMA-9M</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">4096</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">128</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A0.T11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.9B Tokens<sup id="A0.T11.2.1.8.7.1" class="ltx_sup">*</sup></td></tr>
<tr id="A0.T11.2.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Language Modeling</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">LLaMA-60M</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">128</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">512</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.T11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.9.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">6B Tokens<sup id="A0.T11.2.1.9.7.1" class="ltx_sup">*</sup></td></tr>
<tr id="A0.T11.2.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Language Modeling</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">LLaMA-350M</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">16</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1024</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.T11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.10.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">14.7B Tokens<sup id="A0.T11.2.1.10.7.1" class="ltx_sup">*</sup></td></tr>
<tr id="A0.T11.2.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Language Modeling</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">LLaMA-1B</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">4</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1024</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">512</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A0.T11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.11.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">42B Tokens<sup id="A0.T11.2.1.11.7.1" class="ltx_sup">*</sup></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="A0.T11.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_parbox ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:397.5pt;"><sup id="A0.T11.3.1" class="ltx_sup">*</sup>We use the WikiText dataset. Training duration is calculated based on parameter count (100x for models <math id="A0.T11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>350M, <math id="A0.T11.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 42\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>42</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 42\times</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise). We chose the token count based on <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fishman et al. (2025)</a></cite>, which show that training divergence in low precision usually happen around this amount of tokens relative to model size. Gradient accumulation is used for the 350M and 1B models. The 350M and 1B model configurations where taken directly from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tseng et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p></div></div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.8 </span>Derivation of Proposition 1</h3>

<div id="A0.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The function for a single element is:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}=\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}=\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A0.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A0.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must use the product rule on: <math id="A0.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{1}{s_{q}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{1}{s_{q}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q(s_{q}\cdot\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q(s_{q}\cdot\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\frac{1}{s_{q}}\right)\cdot Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})+\frac{1}{s_{q}}\cdot\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\frac{1}{s_{q}}\right)\cdot Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})+\frac{1}{s_{q}}\cdot\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"></h4>

<div id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Term 1: Derivative of <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{s_{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{s_{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>
This derivative depends on how <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=s(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=s(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left(\frac{1}{s_{q}}\right)=-\frac{1}{s_{q}^{2}}\frac{\partial s_{q}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}^{2}}\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left(\frac{1}{s_{q}}\right)=-\frac{1}{s_{q}^{2}}\frac{\partial s_{q}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}^{2}}\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"></h4>

<div id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Term 2: Derivative of <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>
We apply the chain rule to <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and then the product rule to its argument <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\cdot\frac{\partial(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\cdot\frac{\partial(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\partial s_{q}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)\mathbf{X}_{ij}+s_{q}\left(\frac{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)=\mathbf{X}_{ij}\frac{\partial s_{q}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}=\mathbf{X}_{ij}q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\partial s_{q}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)\mathbf{X}_{ij}+s_{q}\left(\frac{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)=\mathbf{X}_{ij}\frac{\partial s_{q}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}=\mathbf{X}_{ij}q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the full derivative of the second term is:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})=Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\left(\mathbf{X}_{ij}q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})=Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\left(\mathbf{X}_{ij}q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Combining and Final Result</h4>

<div id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We substitute the results for both terms back into the main equation:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\left(-\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}^{2}}\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})+\frac{1}{s_{q}}\left[Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\left(\mathbf{X}_{ij}q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\left(-\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}^{2}}\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})+\frac{1}{s_{q}}\left[Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\left(\mathbf{X}_{ij}q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+s_{q}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Distributing the <math id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{s_{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{s_{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> term:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}^{2}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{s_{q}}Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+\frac{s_{q}}{s_{q}}Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}^{2}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{s_{q}}Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})q^{\prime}(s)\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}+\frac{s_{q}}{s_{q}}Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Grouping the terms by their derivative component gives the final result for this fully general model:</p>
<table id="A0.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})+\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left[\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}}\left(\mathbf{X}_{ij}Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})-\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)\right]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})+\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left[\frac{q^{\prime}(s)}{s_{q}}\left(\mathbf{X}_{ij}Q^{\prime}(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})-\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.9 </span>Theorem 2 derivation</h3>

<div id="A0.SS9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A0.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We want to find the partial derivative of <math id="A0.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to an element <math id="A0.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>. The transformation is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})=g(\mathbf{X})\cdot f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})=g(\mathbf{X})\cdot f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A0.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\mathbf{X})=\text{absmax}(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>absmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\mathbf{X})=\text{absmax}(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{p}=\mathbf{X}_{p}/g(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{p}=\mathbf{X}_{p}/g(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>. An element <math id="A0.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to a specific block <math id="A0.SS9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A0.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A0.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A0.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Apply the Product Rule.</span> We treat <math id="A0.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> as two functions of <math id="A0.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. The product rule states <math id="A0.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(uv)^{\prime}=u^{\prime}v+uv^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(uv)^{\prime}=u^{\prime}v+uv^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\cdot f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+g\cdot\frac{\partial f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\cdot f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+g\cdot\frac{\partial f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A0.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Apply the Chain Rule.</span> The second term’s derivative requires the chain rule because <math id="A0.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A0.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a function of <math id="A0.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\cdot\frac{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\cdot\frac{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A0.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Apply the Quotient Rule.</span> We find the derivative of <math id="A0.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}=\mathbf{X}_{ij}/g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}=\mathbf{X}_{ij}/g</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A0.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> using the quotient rule <math id="A0.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{u}{v})^{\prime}=\frac{u^{\prime}v-uv^{\prime}}{v^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{u}{v})^{\prime}=\frac{u^{\prime}v-uv^{\prime}}{v^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{1\cdot g-\mathbf{X}_{ij}\cdot\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}}{g^{2}}=\frac{1}{g}-\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g^{2}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{1\cdot g-\mathbf{X}_{ij}\cdot\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}}{g^{2}}=\frac{1}{g}-\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g^{2}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A0.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Substitute and Combine.</span> Now, substitute the result from step (3) into step (2), and then the result of that into step (1).</p>
<table id="A0.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+g\cdot\left[\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\left(\frac{1}{g}-\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g^{2}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+g\cdot\left[\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\left(\frac{1}{g}-\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g^{2}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A0.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simplify and Rearrange.</span> Distribute the outer <math id="A0.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> into the brackets.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+\frac{g}{g}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}-\frac{g\cdot\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g^{2}}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+\frac{g}{g}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}-\frac{g\cdot\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g^{2}}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.I2.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The terms simplify, and we can replace <math id="A0.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>g</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}}{g}</annotation></semantics></math> with its definition, <math id="A0.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}-\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})+\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}-\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.I2.i5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Finally, we group the terms containing <math id="A0.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math> to arrive at the theorem’s statement.</p>
<table id="A0.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}+\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left(f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})-\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}+\frac{\partial g}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left(f_{ij}(\mathbf{U}_{p})-\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}\frac{\partial f_{ij}}{\partial\mathbf{U}_{p,ij}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A0.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.10 </span>Propostion 1 Proof</h3>

<div id="A0.SS10.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A0.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows directly from applying the chain rule to <math id="A0.SS10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(Z(\mathbf{X}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(Z(\mathbf{X}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{ds}{dZ}\cdot\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{d}{dZ}\left(\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z}\right)\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4 max</mtext><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4 max</mtext><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{ds}{dZ}\cdot\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{d}{dZ}\left(\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z}\right)\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.11 </span>Absmax gradient derivation</h3>

<div id="A0.SS11.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A0.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A0.SS11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{*},j^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{*},j^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> be the index of the element with the maximum absolute value, such that <math id="A0.SS11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\mathbf{X})=|\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\mathbf{X})=|\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}}|</annotation></semantics></math>. We first find the gradient of <math id="A0.SS11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>. The derivative of the absolute value function is the sign function, <math id="A0.SS11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d|x|}{dx}=\sign(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d|x|}{dx}=\sign(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. The derivative is non-zero only when we differentiate with respect to the element <math id="A0.SS11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself. This can be expressed precisely using the Kronecker delta:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial|\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}}|}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\sign(\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}})\cdot\delta_{ii^{*}}\delta_{jj^{*}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\frac{\partial|\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}}|}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\sign(\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}})\cdot\delta_{ii^{*}}\delta_{jj^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this result into the formula from Theorem 2 completes the proof.</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\text{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\text{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\left(\sign(\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}})\cdot\delta_{ii^{*}}\delta_{jj^{*}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mtext>FP4 max</mtext><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mtext>FP4 max</mtext><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\text{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\text{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\left(\sign(\mathbf{X}_{i^{*}j^{*}})\cdot\delta_{ii^{*}}\delta_{jj^{*}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS11.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS11.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.12 </span>Softmax gradient derivation</h3>

<div id="A0.SS12.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A0.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first find the gradient of <math id="A0.SS12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> by applying the chain rule multiple times.</span></p>
<table id="A0.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left[\frac{1}{\beta}\log\left(\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left[\frac{1}{\beta}\log\left(\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\cdot\frac{1}{\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left(e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{ij}|}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\cdot\frac{1}{\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}\left(e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{ij}|}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\cdot\frac{1}{\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}}\cdot\left(e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{ij}|}\cdot\beta\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\cdot\frac{1}{\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}}\cdot\left(e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{ij}|}\cdot\beta\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{ij}|}}{\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}}\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{ij}|}}{\sum_{k,l}e^{\beta|\mathbf{X}_{kl}|}}\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The fractional term is the definition of the softmax function applied to the scaled, absolute values of the tensor elements. Thus:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\mathrm{softmax}(\beta|\mathbf{X}|)_{ij}\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=\mathrm{softmax}(\beta|\mathbf{X}|)_{ij}\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS12.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS12.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this dense gradient back into the formula from Theorem 2 completes the proof.</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\left(\mathrm{softmax}(\beta|\mathbf{X}|)_{ij}\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4 max</mtext><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4 max</mtext><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial s}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\mathbf{X}_{ij}}=-\frac{\texttt{FP4 max}}{Z(\mathbf{X})^{2}}\left(\mathrm{softmax}(\beta|\mathbf{X}|)_{ij}\cdot\sign(\mathbf{X}_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS12.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.SS12.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.13 </span>Tensor reconstruction error with MXFP4 format</h3>

<section id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reconstruction error</h4>

<div id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first consider the reconstruction error, i.e., <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{X}-\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\cdot\mathbf{X})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{X}-\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\cdot\mathbf{X})|</annotation></semantics></math> for different choices of <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, rounding modes of <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, block sizes, and max functions <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>. We illustrate different slices of the relative error <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|\mathbf{X}-\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\cdot\mathbf{X})|}{|\mathbf{X}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|\mathbf{X}-\frac{1}{s_{q}}Q(s_{q}\cdot\mathbf{X})|}{|\mathbf{X}|}</annotation></semantics></math>. Figure <a href="#A0.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Reconstruction error ‣ .13 Tensor reconstruction error with MXFP4 format ‣ Elucidating the Design Space of FP4 training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows the reconstruction error for the Straight-Through Estimator (STE) as a function of block size. As expected, the error decreases as the block size increases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/plot_exp1_ste_vs_block_size_median.svg" id="A0.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>E4M3 vs E8M0</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/x23.svg" id="A0.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>E8M0 vs UE5M3</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Reconstruction error using STE as a function of block size.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment 2: STE Error vs. Tensor Scale</h4>

<div id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A0.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Experiment 2: STE Error vs. Tensor Scale ‣ .13 Tensor reconstruction error with MXFP4 format ‣ Elucidating the Design Space of FP4 training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> illustrates the impact of the input tensor’s scale on the STE reconstruction error, plotted on a log-log scale. These plots show comparisons for a fixed block size of 16.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F12.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/plot_exp2_ste_vs_tensor_scale_log_y_median.svg" id="A0.F12.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>E4M3 vs E8M0</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F12.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/x24.svg" id="A0.F12.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>E8M0 vs UE5M3</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Reconstruction error using STE as a function of tensor scale (Block Size = 16).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment 3: Softmax Error vs. Block Size</h4>

<div id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the first experiment, Figure <a href="#A0.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Experiment 3: Softmax Error vs. Block Size ‣ .13 Tensor reconstruction error with MXFP4 format ‣ Elucidating the Design Space of FP4 training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> shows the reconstruction error for the Softmax approximation as a function of block size, comparing different data formats.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F13.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/plot_exp3_softmax_vs_block_size_median.svg" id="A0.F13.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>E4M3 vs E8M0</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F13.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/x25.svg" id="A0.F13.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>E8M0 vs UE5M3</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Reconstruction error using Softmax approximation as a function of block size.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment 4: Softmax Error vs. Tensor Scale</h4>

<div id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A0.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ Experiment 4: Softmax Error vs. Tensor Scale ‣ .13 Tensor reconstruction error with MXFP4 format ‣ Elucidating the Design Space of FP4 training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> shows the effect of tensor scale on the Softmax approximation for a fixed block size of 16 and a <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> value of 40.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F14.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/plot_exp4_softmax_vs_tensor_scale_log_y_median.svg" id="A0.F14.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>E4M3 vs E8M0</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F14.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/x26.svg" id="A0.F14.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>E8M0 vs UE5M3</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span>Reconstruction error using Softmax approximation as a function of tensor scale (Block Size = 16, <math id="A0.F14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=40</annotation></semantics></math>).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment 5: Softmax Sensitivity to <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, Figure <a href="#A0.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ Experiment 5: Softmax Sensitivity to 𝛽 ‣ .13 Tensor reconstruction error with MXFP4 format ‣ Elucidating the Design Space of FP4 training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> analyzes the sensitivity of the Softmax approximation to the inverse temperature parameter, <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. The comparison highlights how tuning <math id="A0.SS13.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> affects the reconstruction error for different formats.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F15" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F15.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/plot_exp5_softmax_vs_beta_median.svg" id="A0.F15.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>E4M3 vs E8M0</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A0.F15.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.17791v1/x27.svg" id="A0.F15.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/366;" width="548" height="366"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>E8M0 vs UE5M3</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span>Reconstruction error using Softmax approximation as a function of the <math id="A0.F15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> parameter.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS14" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.14 </span>Things we tried but didn’t work</h3>

<section id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conditional Block-wise Scaling</h4>

<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As scaling factors have limited range, we found in our initial experiments that the <span id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E4M3</span> format tends to stall during training, which is caused by underflow due to its limited range compared to <span id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E8M0</span>. We propose a conditional scaling strategy, where the choice is determined by comparing the dynamic range of the data’s scales, <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{DR}_{\text{data}}=\frac{g}{\tilde{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>DR</mtext><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{DR}_{\text{data}}=\frac{g}{\tilde{g}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the intrinsic dynamic range of the target scale format, <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{DR}_{\text{format}}=\frac{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>DR</mtext><mtext>format</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{DR}_{\text{format}}=\frac{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\max_{p}\{m_{p}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\max_{p}\{m_{p}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{g}=\min_{p}\{m_{p}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{g}=\min_{p}\{m_{p}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1: <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{DR}_{\text{data}}\leq\text{DR}_{\text{format}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>DR</mtext><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mtext>DR</mtext><mtext>format</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{DR}_{\text{data}}\leq\text{DR}_{\text{format}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Ideal Multiplicative Scaling)</h4>

<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the data’s dynamic range fits within the format’s range, we can compute a single constant <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> using the geometric mean to center the scales within the target range:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\frac{\sqrt{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}\cdot{\tilde{g}}\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}}\cdot{g}}}{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msqrt><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\frac{\sqrt{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}\cdot{\tilde{g}}\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}}\cdot{g}}}{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The full forward pass for an element, including the final de-normalization, is:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})=\frac{C}{q(C\cdot s_{p})}Q\left(\frac{q(C\cdot s_{p})}{C}\cdot\mathbf{X}_{ij}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})=\frac{C}{q(C\cdot s_{p})}Q\left(\frac{q(C\cdot s_{p})}{C}\cdot\mathbf{X}_{ij}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the quantization function for the scales (e.g., rounding to the nearest <span id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E4M3</span> value).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2: <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{DR}_{\text{data}}&gt;\text{DR}_{\text{format}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>DR</mtext><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mtext>DR</mtext><mtext>format</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{DR}_{\text{data}}&gt;\text{DR}_{\text{format}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Affine Mapping fallback)</h4>

<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the scaled dynamic range is too wide, we resort to using an affine transformation to map <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{p}\in[\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g},\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{\tilde{g}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{p}\in[\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g},\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{\tilde{g}}]</annotation></semantics></math> to the range <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}},\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}},\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}]</annotation></semantics></math>. The affine parameters are:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\frac{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}-\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}}}{\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{\tilde{g}}-\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g}},\quad b=\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}-a\cdot\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{\tilde{g}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>g</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\frac{\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}-\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{min}}}{\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{\tilde{g}}-\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g}},\quad b=\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}-a\cdot\frac{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{\tilde{g}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The scale to be quantized is <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{p}=a\cdot s_{p}+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{p}=a\cdot s_{p}+b</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then combine this with tensor scaling to achieve a reasonable quantisation:</p>
<table id="A0.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})=\frac{g\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}\cdot q(\tilde{s}_{p})}Q\left(q(\tilde{s}_{p})\cdot\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}\cdot\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{ij}(\mathbf{X})=\frac{g\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}{\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}\cdot q(\tilde{s}_{p})}Q\left(q(\tilde{s}_{p})\cdot\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}\cdot\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the above setting, we’re mapping the scale <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> to the full range of <span id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E4M3</span>, however due to the affine mapping we may lose precision for cases when <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{p}\ll g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{p}\ll g</annotation></semantics></math>, since the term <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}\cdot\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E4M3</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbf{X}_{ij}\cdot\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}}{g\cdot\texttt{E4M3}_{\text{max}}}</annotation></semantics></math> will not have the full <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">FP4</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{FP4}_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> range. We motivate this trade-off with the observation that <span id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NVFP4</span> has a block-size of 16, implying that having a well-represented scale outweighs the block accuracy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When we tested the above on CIFAR10 as a unit test for <span id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E4M3</span> we couldn’t get anywhere near convergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sigmoid approximation</h4>

<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\{v_{1},\dots,v_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\{v_{1},\dots,v_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote FP4 (E2M1) levels. Define intervals <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}=(v_{i},v_{i+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}=(v_{i},v_{i+1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, with</p>
<table id="A0.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=\frac{v_{i}+v_{i+1}}{2},\quad\Delta_{i}=v_{i+1}-v_{i},\quad\gamma_{i}=\frac{12}{\Delta_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=\frac{v_{i}+v_{i+1}}{2},\quad\Delta_{i}=v_{i+1}-v_{i},\quad\gamma_{i}=\frac{12}{\Delta_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in I_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in I_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A0.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}(x)=\frac{(x-c_{i})\gamma_{i}}{T},\quad w(x)=\sigma(z_{i}(x))=\frac{1}{1+e^{-z_{i}(x)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}(x)=\frac{(x-c_{i})\gamma_{i}}{T},\quad w(x)=\sigma(z_{i}(x))=\frac{1}{1+e^{-z_{i}(x)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smooth Quantization Properties)<span id="Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as above. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A0.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A0.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A0.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The forward mapping </span><math id="A0.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)=v_{i}+w(x)\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)=v_{i}+w(x)\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a smooth interpolation between </span><math id="A0.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A0.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> using a sigmoid.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A0.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Its derivative is</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(x)=\Delta_{i}\cdot\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))\cdot\frac{\gamma_{i}}{T}=\frac{12}{T}\,\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(x)=\Delta_{i}\cdot\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))\cdot\frac{\gamma_{i}}{T}=\frac{12}{T}\,\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A0.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the limit </span><math id="A0.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A0.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> converges to the standard ties-to-even quantization:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{T\to 0}Q(x)=\begin{cases}v_{i},&amp;x\leq c_{i}\\
v_{i+1},&amp;x&gt;c_{i}\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{T\to 0}Q(x)=\begin{cases}v_{i},&amp;x\leq c_{i}\\
v_{i+1},&amp;x&gt;c_{i}\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The forward mapping is linear in <math id="Thmproposition3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with a weight <math id="Thmproposition3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(x)\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(x)\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> from the sigmoid, so it is smooth and bounded by <math id="Thmproposition3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the derivative:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(x)=\frac{d}{dx}\big(v_{i}+w(x)\Delta_{i}\big)=\Delta_{i}\frac{dw}{dx}=\Delta_{i}\frac{dw}{dz_{i}}\frac{dz_{i}}{dx}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(x)=\frac{d}{dx}\big(v_{i}+w(x)\Delta_{i}\big)=\Delta_{i}\frac{dw}{dx}=\Delta_{i}\frac{dw}{dz_{i}}\frac{dz_{i}}{dx}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Thmproposition3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\sigma(z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\sigma(z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmproposition3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dw}{dz_{i}}=\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dw}{dz_{i}}=\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmproposition3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dz_{i}/dx=\gamma_{i}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dz_{i}/dx=\gamma_{i}/T</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}(x)=\Delta_{i}\cdot\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))\cdot\frac{\gamma_{i}}{T}=\frac{12}{T}\,\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}(x)=\Delta_{i}\cdot\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i}))\cdot\frac{\gamma_{i}}{T}=\frac{12}{T}\,\sigma(z_{i})(1-\sigma(z_{i})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, as <math id="Thmproposition3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the sigmoid becomes a step function at <math id="Thmproposition3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\Big(\frac{(x-c_{i})\gamma_{i}}{T}\Big)\to\begin{cases}0,&amp;x&lt;c_{i}\\
1,&amp;x&gt;c_{i}\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\Big(\frac{(x-c_{i})\gamma_{i}}{T}\Big)\to\begin{cases}0,&amp;x&lt;c_{i}\\
1,&amp;x&gt;c_{i}\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="Thmproposition3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to ties-to-even quantization:</span></p>
<table id="A0.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)\to\begin{cases}v_{i},&amp;x\leq c_{i}\\
v_{i+1},&amp;x&gt;c_{i}\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)\to\begin{cases}v_{i},&amp;x\leq c_{i}\\
v_{i+1},&amp;x&gt;c_{i}\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We tried this gradient adjustment, we expected it would provide a significant performance benefit, however this was not the case in early experiments (MNIST, gaussian regression, CIFAR10, llama 9M). Hence on lower level implementations, the additional complexity is not justified. The additional complexity is <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(np\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(np\log k)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> extra memory. <math id="A0.SS14.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of polynomials used to evaluate the exponential function used in the sigmoid.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
